# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template, which holds names and no values. It is the one place
# the required variables are written down, so it has to travel with the code.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Claude Code worktrees
.claude/worktrees/

# Anything named *.local.md is this copy's own and never ships.
#
# AGENTS.md, DECISIONS.md and NOTES.md are public on purpose — a stranger
# running their own journal needs to know how it is built and why. What does
# not belong in every copy is anything about the person keeping this one:
# how they want things explained, and where they are taking the project.
#
# One pattern rather than a list, so the next one is covered without anybody
# having to remember this file exists.
*.local.md
